<title>MALAYSIA: Rahman Hydraulic suspension extended.</title>
<headline>Rahman Hydraulic suspension extended.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange (KLSE) said on Tuesday it was extending the suspension of trading in the shares of Rahman Hydraulic Tin Bhd by 10 trading days.</p>
<p>The KLSE said in a statement that the extension to June 13, from June 2, was granted to enable Rahman Hydraulic to announce details of equity acquisition in some companies.</p>
<p>&quot;The proposed acquisitions of significant equity in some companies has not been finalised,&quot; the KLSE said in the statement.</p>
<p>The shares have been suspended since April 29.</p>
<p>On May 9, Rahman Hydraulic, a commodities and property company, had said it was acquiring a major equity interest in another company.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
